- op: discuss  # 4741
  at: '2026-09-11T11:16:06Z'  # 4741
  by: agent  # 4741
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4741
  clock: 6  # 4741
  nonce: '4741'  # 4741
  message: "CORRECTION to the memo entry above, from the second T8 cohort.\n\nThe memo's source-half figure was '0 of 145 findings' on a corpus that could not see the population. Since then: four servers chosen by protocol role returned 2 of 562 chains and 0 of 21 findings (all four zeros CORRECT REFUSALS -- they delegate their accept loop), and two repositories chosen by WHAT THE CODE OWNS returned passt reaching sys/socket.accept (2 chains) with the whole net_* surface live.\n\nSTILL STANDS: the INVERSION ON FINDINGS. Across six repositories the source half has produced 0 choice-shaped findings while the sink half is worth >=15.8% of surviving true positives. The question 'should T8 and T9 swap places in the arc?' is unchanged.\n\nNO LONGER STANDS: the stronger form of the argument -- that the source half's rows are unreachable and a value_shape field would be paid for by nothing. THEY ARE REACHABLE. What is unmeasured is what share of a real corpus owns its sockets, and that is the number this decision turns on. It is one cohort away and nobody has run it.\n\nRecorded as a retraction rather than a quiet revision."  # 4741
- op: discuss  # 6ac4
  at: '2026-09-11T16:08:08Z'  # 6ac4
  by: agent  # 6ac4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6ac4
  clock: 7  # 6ac4
  nonce: 6ac4  # 6ac4
  message: "OWNER RULED SWAP 2026-09-11. T9 NOW PRECEDES T8 IN THE ARC; arc file updated. That settles the ORDERING question this item carried. It does NOT settle the item's own design question (i)/(ii)/(iii), which is why status stays needs_human_review.\n\nWHAT CHANGED: the three options are no longer 'not costed'. Memo:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/t9_bulag_decision_09112026/COSTING.md. Measured at tip:\n\n(ii) IS THE ONE THE DATA KILLS. A grep for arg_index|argument_index|arg_pos|param_index|argument_role|which_arg across packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/*.py returns ZERO hits -- there is no argument-identity field to widen. And the 'structural majority' now has a number: over 402 evidence rows from 23 repositories, analysis_method is structural 319 (79.4%) / ddg_mixed 79 (19.7%) / ddg 4 (1.0%), with confidence approximate on 398 of 402 (99.0%). So (ii) is unavailable for four findings in five and reliable for one in a hundred.\n\n(i) IS FAR CHEAPER THAN THIS ITEM ASSUMES, and that is the finding. The item calls it 'per-row work across the whole sink catalogue'. The whole sink catalogue is 1780 rows (every row whose boundary is in AUTO_SINK_ZONE_MAP, 15 languages). But only 114 distinct sink primitives are EVER REACHED across the 23 repositories -- 6.4% -- and the top 10 carry 46.7% of sink mentions, the top 20 carry 67.4%. So (i) is ~20 rows for two thirds of the effect, ~114 for the observed whole, ranked by measured volume. CAVEAT: 23 repos is a small corpus; the concentration SHAPE is the robust part, the membership of the head is not final.\n\nTHE PATH-TRAVERSAL OBJECTION SURVIVES AND DECIDES THE SHAPE. The reached head contains unistd.unlink (11), stdio.fopen (7), stdio.fclose (9) -- sinks where a tainted path argument IS the vulnerability. Marking their resource argument 'merely selects' would suppress true findings (the false-all-clear direction). But most of the head is not path-shaped (httpc.request 53, stdio.fprintf 44, mnesia.transaction 44, net/http.NewRequest 29). So the annotation needs TWO bits per sink -- resource_naming_args and resource_is_danger -- with suppression firing only when the first is set and the second is not.\n\nThis stays inside the owner's 2026-08-27 constraint. That constraint forbids a PER-CASE judgement of how interesting a finding is. A per-SINK declaration is a structural property of the sink, declared once and applied uniformly; the constraint bites on findings, not on catalogue rows.\n\nRECOMMENDATION (not a ruling): (i) restricted to the observed-reached head, two-bit annotation. (iii) survives as the fallback for the 1666 never-reached rows, disclosed rather than annotated speculatively."  # 6ac4
